start
if (Current nondeleted queued pair, dispatch due?) then (yes)
 :repair_work: lock/recheck;\nmissing work row -> stage stable ID;\nsent + no claim token -> rearm;\notherwise publisher retains it;
 :advance next_dispatch_at; COMMIT;\nrelay; SAME Attempt UUID;
else (no)
 if (Execution interruption eligible?) then (yes)
  :lock_pair + processing-state recheck;\ninterrupt -> abandoned Attempt / failed Job;\ncleanup + result; COMMIT;
  :relay failed result; Media projects it;\nowner retry -> NEW Attempt UUID;
 else (no)
  :No recovery mutation;
 endif
endif
stop
legend bottom
Interruption eligible = current nondeleted processing pair AND (expired lease/deadline OR matched STOPPED).
Queued repair restores delivery intent; interruption waits for owner retry. 120s is a target, not measured latency.
endlegend
